# llm-step's dependencies (format `<path> <name>`, path relative to this dir):
# the rustc worker factory that compiles it, the opt-in Git runner it executes
# on, the llm-client and conversation-protocol crates it links, and THE TOOLS
# IT DRIVES — bash-tool, rgrep, bash (the tree-tool shell), merge, the caos
# build/test tools (caos-build, caos-test — moved out of caos-tools/ so the
# harness offers them ALWAYS from its own version) and run-and-update-ref. LOCAL
# deps (mounted under DEEP-DEPS/ by deepening) rather than /std, so std has no
# ambient self-reference.
#
# The tools are declared HERE, rather than by whoever calls llm-step, because
# they are llm-step's dependencies: the caller should say what the turn is, not
# which shell the agent greps with. `.caos-expr` binds them, so resolving
# llm-step yields a step image with its tools already attached.
